-mesh","label":"Faults and patch-refinement of the mesh","html_id":"faults-and-patch-refinement-of-the-mesh","implicit":true,"key":"VbWrBpg8Qb"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-entry-summary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A slipping fault is a discontinuity the mesh has to represent, along a trace that moves as the model runs. We build the fault into a short-lived mesh made from a static base. The base holds the state, the partition and the coarse multigrid levels; the add-on is a copy of the base's finest level with the fault placed into it as a narrow structured band, split along the fault, and rebuilt from the base whenever the fault moves.","key":"JgmO4YCRVq"}],"key":"kC0rXglu2g"}],"key":"jlgke2saAq"}],"key":"R4hriZ99y3"}],"key":"lAtMi94hQQ"}],"key":"tobJ9hbIHU"}],"key":"SK73HTL3hc"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"next":{"title":"Faults and patch-refinement of the mesh","url":"/faults-on-an-add-on-mesh","group":"Underworld Geodynamics"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}